---
import "../styles/diagram.css";
// Homepage block: a computed can own state. Two micro-diagrams, Life and a firefly, then links.
import { href } from "../site";
---
<figure class="dg sn">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 680 150" role="img" aria-label="Left, Game of Life: generation feeds world(prev), which feeds the cells. Right, a firefly: tick and its inbox feed A(prev), which writes into the inbox of B.">
    <defs>
      <marker id="sn-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0L10,5L0,10z" class="dg-ah" /></marker>
      <marker id="sn-w" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0L10,5L0,10z" class="dg-wh" /></marker>
    </defs>
    <text x="10" y="20" class="dg-h">Game of Life</text>
    <rect x="10" y="58" width="100" height="28" class="dg-b" /><text x="60" y="77" text-anchor="middle">generation</text>
    <line x1="110" y1="72" x2="146" y2="72" class="dg-l" marker-end="url(#sn-a)" />
    <rect x="148" y="56" width="104" height="32" class="dg-b solid" /><text x="200" y="77" text-anchor="middle">world(prev)</text>
    <line x1="252" y1="72" x2="288" y2="72" class="dg-l" marker-end="url(#sn-a)" />
    <rect x="290" y="58" width="56" height="28" class="dg-b" /><text x="318" y="77" text-anchor="middle">cells</text>
    <text x="10" y="128" class="dg-s">the world is the computed's own value</text>

    <line x1="366" y1="10" x2="366" y2="140" class="dg-sep" />

    <text x="384" y="20" class="dg-h">a firefly</text>
    <rect x="384" y="38" width="64" height="26" class="dg-b" /><text x="416" y="56" text-anchor="middle">tick</text>
    <rect x="384" y="82" width="64" height="26" class="dg-b" /><text x="416" y="100" text-anchor="middle">inbox</text>
    <line x1="448" y1="51" x2="478" y2="66" class="dg-l" marker-end="url(#sn-a)" />
    <line x1="448" y1="95" x2="478" y2="80" class="dg-l" marker-end="url(#sn-a)" />
    <rect x="480" y="56" width="70" height="32" class="dg-b solid" /><text x="515" y="77" text-anchor="middle">A(prev)</text>
    <line x1="550" y1="72" x2="586" y2="72" class="dg-wl" marker-end="url(#sn-w)" />
    <text x="568" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-s">write</text>
    <rect x="588" y="58" width="84" height="28" class="dg-b" /><text x="630" y="77" text-anchor="middle">inbox B</text>
    <text x="384" y="128" class="dg-s">reads in, messages out</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>Reads form dependencies. Writes carry messages. <code>prev</code> carries local state.</figcaption>
</figure>
<p>One small machine, three kinds of computation. <a href={href("/game-of-life/")}>Game of Life</a>: state evolves, the whole world is one computed. <a href={href("/fireflies/")}>Fireflies</a>: events propagate, and the runtime itself finds the fixpoint. <a href={href("/constraints/")}>Constraints</a>: knowledge converges, until no cell can rule out anything more.</p>
